    "question": {
      ":question/id": "4fcaa245-9177-5bbc-9530-ae775a0ada83",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets does the number $\\frac{1}{\\pi}$ belong?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The number $\\frac{1}{\\pi}$ is a positive irrational number. It is not a rational number.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$ contains the nonnegative real numbers. Therefore, $\\frac{1}{\\pi}$ belongs to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}$ contains all rational numbers. Therefore, $\\frac{1}{\\pi}$ does not belong to $\\mathbb{Q}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$ contains the nonpositive real numbers. Therefore, $\\frac{1}{\\pi}$ does not belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}$ contains all real numbers. Therefore, $\\frac{1}{\\pi}$ belongs to $\\mathbb{R}$.\n\nTherefore, select $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$, $\\mathbb{R}$ only.",
