    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6f90c341-d048-5f21-842e-737f9c57922d",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets do all the integers belong?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We must check whether each set contains all the integers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{N}_0$ contains the nonnegative integers. For instance, $-1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{N}_0$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the integers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}$ contains all rational numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}$ contains all real numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{R}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{C}$ contains all complex numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{C}$.\n\nTherefore, select $\\mathbb{Q}$, $\\mathbb{R}$, $\\mathbb{C}$ only.",
